WEBVTT

cue0149613
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.840
In Israel, yes, and not in America.

cue0149614
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:16.520
So that's why my feelings are that the future of Judaism

cue0149615
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.520
is going to be played in the Middle East.

cue0149616
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.200
Another thing which is interesting,

cue0149617
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.799
and then maybe you have the door closed.

cue0149618
00:00:24.799 --> 00:00:28.040
Somebody closes the door, as soon as Mickey Carey comes,

cue0149619
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.920
he will be coming with a, maybe somebody could close the door.

cue0149620
00:00:34.759 --> 00:00:35.799
Yes, that would be nice.

cue0149621
00:00:39.919 --> 00:00:44.439
I do, you know, talking about Israel and so on,

cue0149622
00:00:44.439 --> 00:00:50.240
the focus of Jews, you see, sometimes we Sepharadim

cue0149623
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.520
don't realize that the ʾAshkenaz,

cue0149624
00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.279
there's a whole revolution happening in the ʾAshkenaz

cue0149625
00:00:56.279 --> 00:00:57.080
world.

cue0149626
00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:58.759
Simply because ʾAshkenaz were separated

cue0149627
00:00:58.759 --> 00:01:01.200
from the Middle East for centuries.

cue0149628
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.520
Now they're going back to the Middle East.

cue0149629
00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.599
And in a way, they're becoming like Sepharadim,

cue0149630
00:01:07.599 --> 00:01:11.760
the new generation.

cue0149631
00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.400
They like Middle Eastern food.

cue0149632
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.279
They like Middle Eastern music.

cue0149633
00:01:17.279 --> 00:01:19.279
And they're becoming acclimatized.

cue0149634
00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.239
So it's something very interesting that's

cue0149635
00:01:21.239 --> 00:01:23.279
going to happen, is happening in the Jewish world.

cue0149636
00:01:23.279 --> 00:01:27.040
All right, now I'm going to begin the lecture.

cue0149637
00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:32.000
Our lecture today deals with the 19th century, which

cue0149638
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.279
is the 1800, which is a period of modernity.

cue0149639
00:01:36.279 --> 00:01:39.320
And the title of the lecture is Sepharadim

cue0149640
00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:46.320
in the 19th Century, Column, New Directions and Old Values,

cue0149641
00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.279
the Crisis of This.

cue0149642
00:01:48.279 --> 00:01:54.320
Now let me begin by making a very radical statement.

cue0149643
00:01:54.320 --> 00:02:00.040
The Shabbatai Sevii movement transformed

cue0149644
00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.879
the whole map of Judaism.

cue0149645
00:02:02.879 --> 00:02:07.760
Whatever the Jew was before Shabbatai Sevii,

cue0149646
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.839
that Jew was connected with the Middle Ages,

cue0149647
00:02:10.839 --> 00:02:14.720
with Maranakadosh, Halakha, Reef, Rambam,

cue0149648
00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:20.360
Rosh, with a whole tradition in which the text and law.

cue0149649
00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.960
It makes a difference when you say Sepharadim, ʾAshkenaz.

cue0149650
00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:30.559
The text and the Halakha were the center of your life.

cue0149651
00:02:30.559 --> 00:02:36.600
The Shabbatai Sevii movement destroyed

cue0149652
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.240
the whole rabbinic establishment.

cue0149653
00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.479
Why and how?

cue0149654
00:02:41.479 --> 00:02:44.559
On two very important bases.

cue0149655
00:02:44.559 --> 00:02:50.759
Number one, most of the rabbis, and that's a fact,

cue0149656
00:02:50.759 --> 00:02:53.559
they either supported Shabbatai Sevii

cue0149657
00:02:53.559 --> 00:02:57.080
or kept quiet about Shabbatai Sevii.

cue0149658
00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:59.440
And there were very, very few rabbis

cue0149659
00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.639
who attacked Shabbatai Sevii.

cue0149660
00:03:01.639 --> 00:03:04.160
By few, I would say maybe 10.

cue0149661
00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:07.520
In qabbala, it was Rabbi Yaʿaqoḇ Semach attacked him,

cue0149662
00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.520
showing that he was wrong.

cue0149663
00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.759
There was people like Rabbi Yaʿaqoḇ Sasportas,

cue0149664
00:03:11.759 --> 00:03:14.759
was from England, Sepharadi from England.

cue0149665
00:03:14.759 --> 00:03:17.320
Talk about the Sepharadim, about ʾAshkenaz.

cue0149666
00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.880
There were people like Rabbi Yaʿaqoḇ Hages,

cue0149667
00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.559
originally from Morocco, then in Israel.

cue0149668
00:03:22.559 --> 00:03:25.679
And Rabbi Aaron LaPapa.

cue0149669
00:03:25.679 --> 00:03:26.720
There were a few rabbis.

cue0149670
00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:33.440
Rabbi Yoseph Ergas, also in qabbala, from Livorno.

cue0149671
00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:37.279
There were a few rabbis who attacked him.

cue0149672
00:03:37.279 --> 00:03:40.639
ʾAshkenaz, of course, there were the famous Yaʿaqoḇ Emdin

cue0149673
00:03:40.639 --> 00:03:45.720
in Amsterdam, who attacked the Shabbatai.

cue0149674
00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:51.320
But most of the rabbis were either acquiesced,

cue0149675
00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:55.639
went along, or participated.

cue0149676
00:03:55.639 --> 00:04:00.520
And therefore, when the end of Shabbatai Sevii,

cue0149677
00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:04.399
with its conversion to Islam, came about,

cue0149678
00:04:04.399 --> 00:04:09.919
this brought a total collapse of the trust

cue0149679
00:04:09.919 --> 00:04:14.279
that existed for centuries between the Jewish public

cue0149680
00:04:14.279 --> 00:04:15.679
and the rabbinic establishment.

cue0149681
00:04:15.679 --> 00:04:18.000
That's number one.

cue0149682
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.279
Number two, another reason is that Shabbatai Sevii,

cue0149683
00:04:22.279 --> 00:04:26.399
when he was proclaiming his messianship,

cue0149684
00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:32.279
he was doing it on the basis of the most valued

cue0149685
00:04:32.279 --> 00:04:35.200
element in Judaism, qabbala.

cue0149686
00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.399
The Kabbalat HaAri.

cue0149687
00:04:37.399 --> 00:04:42.040
Now, of course, he was wrong.

cue0149688
00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:45.799
Of course, he was misrepresenting the qabbala.

cue0149689
00:04:45.799 --> 00:04:49.720
But the fact that something which is so precious,

cue0149690
00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:54.839
like qabbala, could have been manipulated,

cue0149691
00:04:54.839 --> 00:05:00.399
already put the Jew as a kind of a warning to the Jew.

cue0149692
00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:07.200
And they mistrusted both the rabbis as an establishment

cue0149693
00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.600
and the tradition transmitted by the rabbis,

cue0149694
00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:11.880
like, for instance, the qabbala.

cue0149695
00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.160
These are the two things.

cue0149696
00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.839
Now, what happened?

cue0149697
00:05:15.839 --> 00:05:20.519
Let me begin with what happened in the ʾAshkenaz world.

cue0149698
00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:24.839
In the ʾAshkenaz world, the following movement happened.

cue0149699
00:05:24.839 --> 00:05:27.679
Otherwise, you cannot understand what happened with the Jews.

cue0149700
00:05:27.679 --> 00:05:31.760
Number one was the reform.

cue0149701
00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:35.640
You have to understand the reform movement, which

cue0149702
00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:45.440
begins at the end of the 1780s, 1770s, with Moses Mendelssohn.

cue0149703
00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:50.480
You have to understand it not in a vacuum,

cue0149704
00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:55.119
but in light of what happened before with Jabotai Sevi.

cue0149705
00:05:55.119 --> 00:05:59.320
Jews were looking for an alternative.

cue0149706
00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:03.040
One thing many Jews, particularly in Western Europe,

cue0149707
00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:03.959
we're going to see it.

cue0149708
00:06:03.959 --> 00:06:05.600
And this has affected also the Sepharadim.

cue0149709
00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:06.920
We'll see later on.

cue0149710
00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:11.359
They did not trust it, no longer their ability to establish it.

cue0149711
00:06:11.359 --> 00:06:13.279
They were looking for an alternative.

cue0149712
00:06:13.279 --> 00:06:20.279
Moses Mendelssohn, rightly or wrongly, I think wrongly,

cue0149713
00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:23.239
he offered an alternative.

cue0149714
00:06:23.239 --> 00:06:26.320
Now, we're going to see later on why this alternative became so appealing

cue0149715
00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.279
later on.

cue0149716
00:06:28.279 --> 00:06:30.160
But he offered an alternative.

cue0149717
00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.880
So the first thing that you have there

cue0149718
00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:37.040
is you have the reform movement that appeared

cue0149719
00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:42.399
in Western ʾAshkenaz communities.

cue0149720
00:06:42.399 --> 00:06:51.559
Second, a reaction to the reform movement was a new movement.

cue0149721
00:06:51.559 --> 00:06:55.600
If you would have used the word Orthodox in the 1750s,

cue0149722
00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.559
nobody would understand how could we be an Orthodox Jew.

cue0149723
00:06:58.559 --> 00:06:59.760
They didn't understand this.

cue0149724
00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:00.600
Why not?

cue0149725
00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:03.239
The word Orthodox always appears with the Christians.

cue0149726
00:07:03.239 --> 00:07:05.320
It's an Orthodox church.

cue0149727
00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:08.040
A Jew, Shomer Mesroth, in our language, for instance,

cue0149728
00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:14.160
in our Arabic, Nasmalah, Shomer Mesroth, Bichafd Rabbo, yes?

cue0149729
00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.519
I don't know, but also in Ladino,

cue0149730
00:07:16.519 --> 00:07:19.679
we don't have no word for Orthodox.

cue0149731
00:07:19.679 --> 00:07:22.959
We don't have no word for Orthodox in Ladino.

cue0149732
00:07:22.959 --> 00:07:24.040
We don't have it.

cue0149733
00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.959
There isn't.

cue0149734
00:07:25.959 --> 00:07:32.119
Now, Orthodoxy, you have to understand it very well.

cue0149735
00:07:32.119 --> 00:07:36.480
It's something also as a reaction to Shabbatai Sevi.

cue0149736
00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:37.279
How?

cue0149737
00:07:37.279 --> 00:07:42.480
Well, Shabbatai Sevi had wrong ideas.

cue0149738
00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.720
The doctrines of Shabbatai Sevi are wrong.

cue0149739
00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:50.880
Come the Orthodoxy and say, well, they're right doctrines.

cue0149740
00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:53.160
What are the right ideas?

cue0149741
00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:57.239
What are the right values?

cue0149742
00:07:57.239 --> 00:08:02.640
And put the emphasis on belief, on ideology.

cue0149743
00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:06.679
Traditionally, that was not the case.

cue0149744
00:08:06.679 --> 00:08:07.920
You don't put ideas.

cue0149745
00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.119
The question is, how you behave?

cue0149746
00:08:11.959 --> 00:08:14.160
Does he put the filling?

cue0149747
00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.040
Does he come twice?

cue0149748
00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:20.679
Does he salivate with minyan or doesn't salivate with minyan?

cue0149749
00:08:20.679 --> 00:08:21.920
Does he eat kashar?

cue0149750
00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:22.920
He doesn't eat kashar.

cue0149751
00:08:23.679 --> 00:08:28.679
His beliefs, between him and his maker,

cue0149752
00:08:28.679 --> 00:08:30.720
nobody knows about this.

cue0149753
00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:33.840
But now they put a new emphasis.

cue0149754
00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:37.200
The emphasis is on beliefs.

cue0149755
00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.559
And in a very interesting way, just like among the Shabbatai,

cue0149756
00:08:41.559 --> 00:08:44.440
you had divided the world into two.

cue0149757
00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:47.080
Those who believe the right beliefs,

cue0149758
00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:50.239
in the case, believe in him.

cue0149759
00:08:50.239 --> 00:08:52.440
And those who do not believe in him,

cue0149760
00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:54.119
and they are the kofrim.

cue0149761
00:08:54.119 --> 00:09:00.479
In a sense, yes, the Orthodox movement

cue0149762
00:09:00.479 --> 00:09:02.440
follows the same ideology.

cue0149763
00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:06.840
You have two kinds of Jews, kofrim and maaminim.

cue0149764
00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.719
Traditionally, both among Sepharadim and ʾAshkenaz,

cue0149765
00:09:09.719 --> 00:09:14.400
prior to Shabbat Yosemite, there was not two classes of Jews.

cue0149766
00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:19.559
I mean, there were a whole spectrum of color.

cue0149767
00:09:19.559 --> 00:09:21.400
In the top, there is white.

cue0149768
00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:22.640
In the bottom, there is black.

cue0149769
00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.880
And there's all the shades in between.

cue0149770
00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:26.679
There was no such a thing as a division

cue0149771
00:09:26.679 --> 00:09:33.719
between two classes of Jews, maaminim and kofrim.

cue0149772
00:09:33.719 --> 00:09:37.159
Therefore, in that sense, Orthodoxy

cue0149773
00:09:37.159 --> 00:09:43.239
is, again, a reaction to both the Reform and this.

cue0149774
00:09:43.239 --> 00:09:48.520
And interesting, just like the Reform movement in the West

cue0149775
00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:52.880
copied the Reform church, and therefore called themselves

cue0149776
00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:56.320
Reform, in Eastern Europe, what's

cue0149777
00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:59.119
the name of the church in Eastern Europe?

cue0149778
00:09:59.119 --> 00:10:02.359
Orthodox, Greek, Russian Orthodox Church.

cue0149779
00:10:02.359 --> 00:10:04.440
They copy the name Orthodox.

cue0149780
00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:05.640
So it's interesting.

cue0149781
00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:08.520
You know, you come, both this.

cue0149782
00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:09.960
Then there is another thing which

cue0149783
00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:13.039
is more profound than that.

cue0149784
00:10:13.039 --> 00:10:15.719
Very interesting.

cue0149785
00:10:15.719 --> 00:10:18.640
Shabbatai Sevi, I want you to understand

cue0149786
00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:22.400
the implications of this man.

cue0149787
00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:27.760
Shabbatai Sevi transformed the role of the Mashiaḥ.

cue0149788
00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.559
What was the traditional role of the Mashiaḥ?

cue0149789
00:10:30.559 --> 00:10:33.359
To be a military leader.

cue0149790
00:10:33.359 --> 00:10:36.479
A military leader who's going to conquer Israel.

cue0149791
00:10:36.479 --> 00:10:38.239
He's going to defeat our enemies.

cue0149792
00:10:38.239 --> 00:10:41.080
And he's going to be able to establish a nation

cue0149793
00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.679
in a geographical spot called Erez Yiśraʾel.

cue0149794
00:10:43.679 --> 00:10:46.039
That is the role of the Mashiaḥ.

cue0149795
00:10:46.039 --> 00:10:51.200
What was the role of the Mashiaḥ in Shabbatai Sevi?

cue0149796
00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.679
He's going to make tikkunim in the ʿolam, the olamot.

cue0149797
00:10:53.679 --> 00:10:56.479
You know, he's going to make tikkunim in the olamot and so on.

cue0149798
00:10:56.479 --> 00:10:58.840
Nothing to do with the redemption,

cue0149799
00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:00.840
with the military redemption of the Jews.

cue0149800
00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:08.840
Both the Reform and the Orthodox grabbed on this point.

cue0149801
00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:09.340
How?

cue0149802
00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:14.900
An extraordinary thing happened.

cue0149803
00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.780
Napoleon.

cue0149804
00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:21.619
Napoleon was one of the most important people

cue0149805
00:11:21.619 --> 00:11:25.580
in forging or helping or promoting

cue0149806
00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.979
the new Jewish identity.

cue0149807
00:11:27.979 --> 00:11:33.099
Napoleon was fascinated by the Jews.

cue0149808
00:11:33.099 --> 00:11:35.219
Was fascinated by the Jews.

cue0149809
00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:41.940
Because he saw in the Jew a supranational organization

cue0149810
00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:44.580
that no European country had at the time.

cue0149811
00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:47.659
As I mentioned last week, if you were a Jew,

cue0149812
00:11:47.659 --> 00:11:51.099
you could make commerce between France and Italy.

cue0149813
00:11:51.099 --> 00:11:53.020
If you were a God, you cannot make commerce

cue0149814
00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:54.500
between France and Italy.

cue0149815
00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:56.659
Because there was no way by which you could

cue0149816
00:11:56.659 --> 00:11:58.900
ensure your contracts and so on.

cue0149817
00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:00.659
There was no supra.

cue0149818
00:12:00.659 --> 00:12:03.580
There was no such thing as an international court.

cue0149819
00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:07.059
Every Bet Din was eased by the finish.

cue0149820
00:12:07.059 --> 00:12:09.299
You put it today, the Bet Din is sha'aret Zion.

cue0149821
00:12:09.299 --> 00:12:10.900
I think that's a good thing.

cue0149822
00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:11.739
It's international.

cue0149823
00:12:11.739 --> 00:12:12.859
How is it international?

cue0149824
00:12:12.859 --> 00:12:16.500
Somebody marries here, escapes to Israel.

cue0149825
00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:20.020
Then comes the Ḥakham Yaʿaqoḇ or Ḥakham Rabbi Hecht

cue0149826
00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:22.380
or Ḥakham Sha'ul, whoever happened to be the Rabbi,

cue0149827
00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:26.659
writes to Israel, grabbed this guy,

cue0149828
00:12:26.659 --> 00:12:29.419
forced him to get to his wife.

cue0149829
00:12:29.419 --> 00:12:31.460
This is an international thing.

cue0149830
00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:34.059
An American court does not have, there

cue0149831
00:12:34.059 --> 00:12:37.500
is no American court that could have this kind of jurisdiction.

cue0149832
00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:39.780
The guy could escape to Argentina.

cue0149833
00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:41.099
They do the same thing.

cue0149834
00:12:41.099 --> 00:12:43.260
Comes from Argentina, goes to Colombia.

cue0149835
00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:44.500
They do the same thing.

cue0149836
00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:50.340
So this kind of organization, supranational organization,

cue0149837
00:12:50.340 --> 00:12:52.340
the government didn't have.

cue0149838
00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:56.739
Napoleon conquered or wanted to conquer the world.

cue0149839
00:12:56.739 --> 00:12:59.419
First reason that he wanted to conquer the world

cue0149840
00:12:59.419 --> 00:13:04.219
was in order to be able to have the whole thing of commerce.

cue0149841
00:13:04.219 --> 00:13:05.979
One of the most interesting thing he did,

cue0149842
00:13:05.979 --> 00:13:07.979
it was the campaign to conquer Erez Israel.

cue0149843
00:13:07.979 --> 00:13:08.820
He went to Palestine.

cue0149844
00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:10.780
You know he went to Palestine.

cue0149845
00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:12.940
Oh, yes.

